# The topics were written against a local bundle of main at 759ef98, made with
# scripts/bundle.sh. The release asset has the same hash, and 759ef98..1609bc2
# changes only README.md and research/min-nightly/ci.sh, so the content is the
# same.
#
# The repin before this one (never published) pinned a local bundle of
# 6c0f7a0 as 0.0.2. Between it and 759ef98 the Roc API changed for app authors
# in: WebSocket (send! adds Infra(SocketErr), close! gives Try({}, [BadCode,
# TooLarge]), Closed has `by`, accept_with!, protocol(s), pick_protocol,
# closed!, extensions, max_queued_bytes; Object.Self.accept_with! takes
# protocols), Worker.new on_trap (Worker.Fixed, Worker.OnTrap),
# Request.query_all and query_pairs (query now parses as URLSearchParams),
# Body.chunk_with! and default_fill, Native.ZstdStream.feed!, Kv.get_with!
# raising cache_ttl_ms to 30 s, Memo checking that a value parses back, one
# clock (the makeHandler option `now` drives Time.now_ms!, Memo, alarms), and
# roc-cbor 0.2.3 in the platform header. 0.0.4 to 0.0.6 change only the test
# helper startApp (js/test.mjs) and docs: the Roc API and the ABI are the same.
#
# A release asset is a public file that `roc check` downloaded into
# the same cache. The bundle has the Roc modules, the production host.wasm and
# the shim js/.
#
# The packages of the platform header: roc-lang/http 2.0.0 and roc-cbor 0.2.3
# (examples/hello_with_cbor.roc has the roc-cbor URL of the header).

# The nightly every app here was checked under, and the manifest's `compiler`
# line. It is compat/last-stack-first-nightly of the platform repo at 759ef98
# (the build of 0.0.6). `plugin validate` needs it unpacked at the repo root as
# roc_nightly-linux_x86_64-2026-11-03-34bd006/. The platform supports
# nightly-2026-10-19-601b54c (min_nightly of js/cfw.json) and later.
compiler nightly-2026-11-03-34bd006

index.json <- the bundle's own .roc modules, parsed by
              `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index`. No source is vendored
examples/  <- examples/hello/main.roc and with_cbor.roc of the platform repo,
              flattened to hello.roc and hello_with_cbor.roc. The one change:
              the platform line `"../../platform/main.roc"` is the URL above.
              (with_cbor.roc has the roc-cbor 0.2.3 URL of the commit 759ef98.)
              The doc comment of hello.roc still says that the line is a path:
              it is upstream's text, kept as it is
topics/    <- this package's own: programs written against this pin and
              declared in plugin.json. The probes that found their comments are
              in research/plugin-probes/ (v2/ for 0.0.1, s_*.roc there for 0.0.2) of the platform repo.
              The 0.0.6 findings (WebSocket close!/send!/Closed, on_trap, Header
              records, the Worker.new literal) came from probes compiled with
              the nightly above; topics/cfw_testing.roc was built to app.wasm
              and its JS test (in its comments) passed under startApp with
              wrangler's Miniflare on Node 26.7
overview.md <- this package's own. Each snippet is in verify/overview-snippets.roc

# What examples/ leaves out, and why:
#   auction   (0.0.2: Gavel.config and Gavel.tables are Memo constants, used as
#             Gavel.config.get!(Gavel.load_config!) and
#             Gavel.tables.get!(Gavel.create_tables!), see the Memo trap)
#             examples/auction is a project of two Workers. web.roc imports the
#             sibling modules Gavel.roc and LotRoom.roc, and the gate compiles
#             one file at a time (`examples/*.roc`, each one an app). A sibling
#             module has no app header, so it cannot sit beside the apps. The
#             skill allows no multi-file example. topics/ has the same
#             patterns in single files (Durable Object, RPC, WebSockets, R2)
# The other files of examples/hello (worker.js, wrangler.toml, README.md,
# .gitignore) are not Roc. topics/cfw_worker.roc and the overview give their
# content. The root talon.toml of the platform repo holds the scripts of the
# examples. A user project has its own talon.toml (overview, "Starting a project").

# What else the repo has and this package does not ship:
#   API.md, MODULES.md, PLAN.md  design and build records of the platform. The
#                topics and the overview give the rules an app author needs
#   conformance/ the test app of the platform. Its routes use each module,
#                but they test the platform, so they are not examples
#   js/          the shim. It is Node code, in the bundle, copied by the user to
#                .roc-cfw/. The plugin ships no code
